<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Ndebele Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1823 CE – 1894 CE (approx.) · capital Bulawayo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Mzilikazi's militarised kingdom, which migrated from the highveld to western Zimbabwe and fell to the British South Africa Company in 1893.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mzilikazi">Mzilikazi</a>, a Khumalo commander under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaka-zulu-king">Shaka</a>, broke away around 1822 with a few hundred followers and moved onto the highveld, absorbing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sotho-tswana-peoples">Sotho-Tswana</a> communities as he went. Defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voortrekkers">Voortrekkers</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/griqua">Griqua</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mosega">Mosega</a> and on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marico-river">Marico</a> in 1837, the Ndebele crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limpopo">Limpopo</a> and rebuilt the kingdom in what is now western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Society was organised in regimental towns, with a ranked order of Zansi of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguni">Nguni</a> origin, Enhla from the highveld and Hole drawn from local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shona">Shona</a>. The king controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and raiding, and Shona chiefdoms paid tribute. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lobengula">Lobengula</a>, who succeeded in 1870, built his capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulawayo">Bulawayo</a> and tried to balance concession-seekers, but the 1888 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudd-concession">Rudd Concession</a> opened the way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cecil-rhodes">Cecil Rhodes</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-south-africa-company">British South Africa Company</a> invaded in 1893, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulawayo">Bulawayo</a> was burnt and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lobengula">Lobengula</a> died in early 1894. The 1896 rising was crushed, and the territory became Matabeleland within <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/company-rule-in-rhodesia">Company rule in Rhodesia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ndebele-kingdom.jpg" alt="Ndebele Kingdom" width="320" height="330"><figcaption>Image: Scanned by Ulamm, modified by Fvasconcellos · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matabeleland.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1823 CE – 1894 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bulawayo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mzilikazi, Lobengula</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ndebele traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>isiNdebele</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a>, <a href="/countries/south-africa">South Africa</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mthwakazi, Matabele Kingdom, Matabeleland</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1858&amp;focus=ndebele-kingdom" aria-label="Ndebele Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5450 2924 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ndebele Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5770 3180L5791 3172M5770 3180L5842 3096M5770 3180L5822 3471"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5791 3172h0M5842 3096h0M5822 3471h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5770 3180h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5770 3180h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bulawayo. <a href="/atlas?year=1858&amp;focus=ndebele-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
